From: Gauthier Piarrette <gauthierpiarrette@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 08:59:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] FXSAVE and XSAVE report MXCSR_MASK 0xFFFF

The mask was 0xFFC0, which tells software that the six status flags cannot be written. A processor with DAZ reports
0x0000FFFF (Intel SDM 11.6.6); AMD adds bit 17 (0x2FFFF). Software that sanitises MXCSR with the mask before LDMXCSR
dropped the flags, and test code skipped values outside it.
---
 FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher/Vector.cpp | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher/Vector.cpp b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher/Vector.cpp
index 89771fb..af15480 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher/Vector.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher/Vector.cpp
@@ -3147,8 +3147,9 @@ void OpDispatchBuilder::SaveSSEState(Ref MemBase) {
 }
 
 void OpDispatchBuilder::SaveMXCSRState(Ref MemBase) {
-  // Store MXCSR and the mask for all bits.
-  _StoreMemPairGPR(OpSize::i32Bit, GetMXCSR(), Constant(0xFFC0), MemBase, 24);
+  // Store MXCSR and MXCSR_MASK, the bits LDMXCSR accepts: 0xFFFF on a processor with DAZ (Intel SDM 11.6.6), the
+  // six status flags included
+  _StoreMemPairGPR(OpSize::i32Bit, GetMXCSR(), Constant(0xFFFF), MemBase, 24);
 }
 
 void OpDispatchBuilder::SaveAVXState(Ref MemBase) {
